# Lite profile: the fewest model calls that still give cited answers and fact-checks.
# Load with:  set -a; . profiles/lite.env; set +a
#
# Model calls per operation with this profile:
#   collection build ............ 0   (BM25 only: no read pass, no embeddings, no Llama Guard)
#   ask --no-llm ................ 0   (verbatim source sentences + passage ids)
#   ask ......................... 1   (0 when gate 1 refuses; repeated questions come from the cache)
#   factcheck (5-8 claims) ...... 7-11  (1-2 extraction + 1 per claim + 1 summary; no --consistency)
#   eval all .................... one per gold question/claim/article, cached on re-runs
#
# Why this is not a quality downgrade on the shipped corpus: README §6, run A (BM25 only) scored
# Q&A 15/16 vs 14/16 for the full configuration, with 0 false "supported" in both.
# What you give up: the read pass helps paraphrased questions on long real documents (README §6).
#
# Only one model to pull (~2.5 GB):  ollama pull qwen3:4b-instruct-2507-q4_K_M
# Ollama settings (where `ollama serve` runs):
#   OLLAMA_FLASH_ATTENTION=1 OLLAMA_KV_CACHE_TYPE=q8_0 OLLAMA_NUM_PARALLEL=1 OLLAMA_MAX_LOADED_MODELS=1
CGPRR_LLM_MODEL=qwen3:4b-instruct-2507-q4_K_M
CGPRR_USE_DENSE=0
CGPRR_READ_PASS=0
CGPRR_GUARD_MODEL=
CGPRR_CACHE=1
CGPRR_NUM_CTX=3072
CGPRR_NUM_PREDICT=768
CGPRR_LLM_CONCURRENCY=1
CGPRR_LLM_TIMEOUT_S=300
CGPRR_QA_MAX_TOKENS=384
CGPRR_QA_PASSAGE_TOKENS=900
CGPRR_KEEP_ALIVE=10m
CGPRR_SLO_ASK_P95_MS=10000
